The product context mentions sched-prod serving about 300k people. That is the service's scale, not a count of affected people. The export counts reports; it does not establish distinct customers, all affected bookings, total losses, or a reliable severity ranking from volume alone.

## Replace subject-only merging with cause review

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and the [triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe) were last reviewed on 2024-06-11. The shared layout marks them stale after the configured half-year threshold. Accepted decisions are immutable: retain 0001 as history and propose a new decision rather than silently rewriting it.

Proposed replacement: resolve the tenant; inspect locale, form version, channel and symptoms; merge only when the cause matches. A subject is a search hint. Matching subjects can hide different causes, and different subjects can describe the same cause. Unknown tenants or inconsistent evidence stay unplaced for review; do not automatically merge them. The executable examples below exercise these distinctions.

<DedupeExplorer />

The app/email pair is the same parser cause despite different subjects. The alder.physio form/app pair has the same subject but different causes. The copper.studio/morrow.tax form pair also has the same subject but different causes. The pale.harbour/alder.physio form pair shares a hint cause despite different subjects. Two unknown senders with matching subjects are not a proven duplicate.

<Callout kind="warn">
The old “merge when unsure” rule can conceal a second problem behind a known ticket. Keep separate cause tickets, document unknowns, and use verified fixes and new intake evidence to decide whether to close them. This proposed workflow needs desk approval before it becomes policy.
</Callout>

## Reproduce and refresh

Run npm ci --ignore-scripts, then npm run build. The .svx imports the export's components, classifier, tenant glob, timeline, layout and RenderStamp rather than transcribing their output. Rendered HTML, CSS and JavaScript are in rendered/. Run npm run preview to see the desk's page at /kb/incidents/4471-split/.

The audit script writes one ID-to-cause assignment per unique merged report to evidence/report-assignments.json. Each ticket links its exact report IDs and the page. Before the next desk handover, refresh the export, rebuild, reconcile counts and flagged evidence, and review the proposed merge rule with the desk.

